Add a services.weatherEnabled option (default true) to Caelestia shell 2.5.0.
Upstream always geolocates through ip-api.com when services.weatherLocation is
empty, from shell startup, the dashboard, and the lock screen's 15-minute
timer; dashboard.showWeather only hides a dashboard tab.  With
weatherEnabled false, the Weather service makes no ip-api, Nominatim, or
Open-Meteo request, ignores replies still in flight, clears fetched data, and
the lock screen weather card and dashboard weather tab are hidden.  Setting it
back to true resumes the upstream flow.

Upstream status: Not submitted; local privacy option.

